Third-party material

AlbumCraft builds embed the default fonts of egui (crate epaint_default_fonts), used for the user
interface and drawn into pictures by the text effect and print captions:

  Ubuntu Light (Ubuntu-Light.ttf) - Ubuntu Font Licence 1.0
  Hack Regular (Hack-Regular.ttf) - MIT License (Copyright 2018 Source Foundry Authors; DejaVu parts public domain)
  Noto Emoji (NotoEmoji-Regular.ttf) - SIL Open Font License 1.1
  emoji-icon-font / egui-icons (emoji-icon-font.ttf, egui-icons.ttf) - MIT License (Copyright 2014 John Slegers)

Their license texts are in the epaint_default_fonts crate (fonts/UFL.txt, fonts/Hack-Regular.txt,
fonts/OFL.txt, fonts/emoji-icon-font-mit-license.txt).

AlbumCraft builds embed map data (assets/geo/, details in assets/geo/README.md):

  Land, lakes and country borders - Natural Earth (naturalearthdata.com), public domain
  World cities (cities15000) - GeoNames (geonames.org), Creative Commons Attribution 4.0

When the user turns online maps on, map pictures and place searches come from OpenStreetMap
(© OpenStreetMap contributors, Open Database License); they are not distributed with AlbumCraft.

All other dependencies are Rust crates under their own licenses (see Cargo.lock; most are MIT
and/or Apache-2.0). Movie export runs the separately installed FFmpeg program, which is not
distributed with AlbumCraft.
